w back to work! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T15:56:33-07:00","id":1252037,"title":"","content":"Heck I was gonna buy mortal remains, but this book is seems too good to pass up. Very excited, hope there is not many errors to deal with while proof reading","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T06:23:07-07:00","id":1252195,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"> Can't wait for this. I am a solid 2e fan yet still find myself gliding to Pandora's Book on rainy days - so to get a new Antagonists book for 2e makes me quite happy. <br /> I do have a question, is there any discussion on Mockeries? Obviously Pandorans have been opened up to be more freeform in 2e (which is a great thing!) but I still design my Pandorans with the idea of a Mockery in mind as a starting point.<br /> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T08:14:11-07:00","id":1252219,"title":"","content":"<b>I do have a question, is there any discussion on Mockeries?</b><br /> <br /> Second Edition makes Pandorans more personal, so _this_ Promethean tries to create _this_ other Promethean and accidentally ends up creating _this_ Pandoran. That's the path we stuck to for Tormented, so no Mockeries there. I do agree that they were quite interesting, but then you'd have a Lineage (of a sort) of Pandorans and I'm not entirely sure that meshes with 2E Pandoran creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Freelance Author and Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1713-mistress-of-whispers","name":"mistress of whispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T10:34:31-07:00","id":1252269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mistress of whispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1120196-night-horrors-the-tormented?p=1252219#post1252219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I do have a question, is there any discussion on Mockeries?</b><br /> <br /> Second Edition makes Pandorans more personal, so _this_ Promethean tries to create _this_ other Promethean and accidentally ends up creating _this_ Pandoran. That's the path we stuck to for Tormented, so no Mockeries there. I do agree that they were quite interesting, but then you'd have a Lineage (of a sort) of Pandorans and I'm not entirely sure that meshes with 2E Pandoran creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there any Pandorans created typically (IE. not via the wildcard that are Firestorms) from sources other than a botched attempt at creating a Promethean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Ven