requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-03T00:38:37-07:00","id":1258683,"title":"","content":"Indeed not Wednesday, but as soon as we can make it. Keep in mind that OPP has a lot of projects in the air.<br /> <br /> Glad you liked Dawn! She really is a tragic monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Freelance Author and Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1713-mistress-of-whispers","name":"mistress of whispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-03T05:20:12-07:00","id":1258702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1120196-night-horrors-the-tormented?p=1258677#post1258677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh? Was it? I know the Zeky's 1e creation required another Zeka to use radiation in the process, but I don't remember anything about other Lineages managing to do the same thing if <i>they</i> used radiation as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, there was a specific generative act for each Lineage, and none of the regular Lineages included radiation. <b>Saturnine Night</b> introduced two things relevant to Dawn: the Zeka, where the generative act included radiation, and rules for demiurges, where the Promethean's creator was something other than another Promethean of the same Lineage. The primary focus of the demiurge section was on mortal demiurges; but it <i>did</i> include non-mortal demiurges, including Prometheans who \u201cmessed with the formula\u201d of the generative act. That's what's going on with Dawn: her \u201cparents\u201d are Promethean demiurges who messed with the formula by introducing radiation into the mix and got a Zeka instead of whatever they were trying to make. <br /> <br /> Demiurges are more of a thing in 2e than they were in 1e; but the notion that your creator doesn't <i>have</i> to be the same Lineage as you was part of the game even back in 1e. In 2e, the nature of the generative act is more important than the nature of the one performing it, and \u201cmessing with the formula\u201d is more likely to work; but that's a change in focus rather than the introduction of something new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><