","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T11:00:13-08:00","id":1265319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1120196-night-horrors-the-tormented?p=1265314#post1265314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this is errata or not, but it strikes me as odd; none of the Promethean characters appear to have Bestowments. I mean, I assume they do, but nothing is listed for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Put it up in Errata anyways if you haven't already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T11:26:27-08:00","id":1265325,"title":"","content":"I like the art.<br /> <br /> I haven't really been able to sit down and read it but I don't normally like art so that's cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T12:09:04-08:00","id":1265345,"title":"","content":"Soooo for those of us who can't afford it until Friday, what's the Jovian?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T12:12:30-08:00","id":1265346,"title":"","content":"It's sort of an anti principle, it wants you not to become a centimani, but to keep your pilgrimage going for as long as possible in stagnation, hoping you will lose hope. Has a ton of possible origins and appears as if it's helpful, when in reality it's just keeping you from advancing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T12:16:12-08:00","id":1265349,"title":"","content":"Neat.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">words are things.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T12:26:57-08:00","id":1265353,"title":"","content":"The Jovian is a manifestation of Azothic Memory with unparalleled control over manifestations of Pyros. It can worsen Disquiet and Wastelands on a whim, awaken Pandorans, turn Pandorans into <i>\u200bsublimati</i> or <i>praecipitati</i>. It cannot be killed (but may feign death to inconvenience a Promethean), though it can perhaps be trapped in a Jovian Athanor (and be passed on like a curse), may be banished by a Promethean it's tied to reaching the New Dawn (and is unleashed once the Redeemed is dead), and Distillations that affect Azothic Memory can trap the Jovian in a Promethean's humours.<br /> <br /> Note that it might be...<br /> <br /> 1) A fallen qashmallim<br /> 2) A former Promethean that's evolved into some kind of thing living in Azothic Memory<br /> 3) It's a Rank 6+ Spirit of Disquiet<br /> 4) It's the manifestation of Torment that has somehow escaped Azothic Memory<br /> 5) It's an Abyssal<br /> 6) It's a God-Machine Angel screwing with the Principle<br /> <br /> EDIT: Note that because the Jovian's omniscience is directly tied to Azothic Memory it might not know <i>anything </i>about Extempore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 11-07-2018, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T12:46:14-08:00","id":1265356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1120196-night-horrors-the-tormented?p=1265353#post1265353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Jovian is a manifestation of Azothic Memory with unparalleled control over manifestations of Pyros. It can worsen Disquiet and Wastelands on a whim, awaken Pandorans, turn Pandorans into <i>\u200bsublimati</i> or <i>praecipitati</i>. It cannot be killed (but may feign death to inconvenience a Promethean), though it can perhaps be trapped in a Jovian Athanor (and be passed on like a curse), may be banished by a Promethean it's tied to reaching the New Dawn (and is unleashed once the Redeemed is dead), and Distillations that affect Azothic Memory can trap the Jovian in a Promethean's humours.<br /> <br /> Note that it might be...<br /> <br /> 1) A fallen qashmallim<br /> 2) A former Promethean that's evolved into some kind of thing living in Azothic Memory<br /> 3) It's a Rank 6+ Spirit of Disquiet<br /> 4) It's the manifestation of Torment that has somehow escaped Azothic Memory<br /> 5) It's an Abyssal<br /> 6) It's a God-Machine Angel screwing with the Principle</div> </div> </div> </div>See, the way y'all feel about the Principle?<br /> <br /> is how I feel about the Jovian.<br /> <br /> Dis gunna be gud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T13:24:23-08:00","id":1265368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1120196-night-horrors-the-tormented?p=1265345#post1265345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo for those of us who can't afford it until Friday, what's the Jovian?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Elpidos are agents of dynamism, and the Lilithim are agents of entropy; then the Jovian is an agents of stasis.<br /> <br /> I like the suggestion it might be a God Machine Angel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-07-2018, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T13:30:03-08:00","id":1265369,"title":"","content":"So the Jovian is against the Centamani, that's interesting.<br /> <br /> Also this is getting quite metaphysical, I likey.<br /> More metaphysical stuff is always good, mage doesn't need to hog it all.<br /> <br /> Now here's hoping Spilled Blood gives a bit of the same to Vamps","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T14:21:06-08:00","id":1265382,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, and the reason Rathbens are called that is because of one Jakob Rathben.<br /> <br /> What you need to know about him is that he left the Cheiron Group...for being blinded by petty medical ethics.<br /> <br /> Let that sink in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-le